-- code.cub — codes of terms as data, and the evaluator as a term: Remark 5.26 “no outer layer”,
-- in §5.5 “What the length counts” of the earlier paper "Respecting Equality", cited in this repository before 2026-11-11 (docs/index.html of the
-- earlier repository avikj/math, last changed 8 Oct 2026, sha256 984fafe88eb6…; no copy is in this repository;
-- its §5 “Complete inference is deterministic and step-optimal” is restated by number in EXPOSITION.md, removed at f00bd0f, readable as git show adaebcd:EXPOSITION.md).
-- The counterpart in the repository's copy of the paper (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf,
-- 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §1.2 “Programs about programs” and
-- §6.2 “Specialization as a program over the language’s own definitions”):
-- "Represented terms form an inductive type Code, with an interpretation eval-g".
-- Variables are de Bruijn indices (words) over one context of term and
-- dimension variables; globals are indices (words) into a signature, data types
-- and their constructors indices into its data part. (code t) writes the code of
-- a source term. eval maps a code to the value the machine gives the term; a
-- question about the evaluator is a term.
data Lst (A : Type) = lnil | lcons (x : A) (xs : Lst A)
